From: Yash Hooda <yash.hooda6@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:56:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add verify.cmd/verify.sh; pin the ruff rule set

One command to rerun the whole folder: install, test, lint, prove
offline, then a demo that teaches a lesson and shows it applied to a
different file. Uses `python -m selfevolve.cli` throughout so it works
without Python's scripts dir on PATH.

`reset` gains --yes. An interactive confirmation prompt is hostile to
scripts and awkward to pipe on Windows.

Pin the ruff rule set explicitly in pyproject, and pin the tool to
>=0.15,<0.17 in CI. Found this by running the new script: ruff 0.16
expanded its default rule set over 0.15 and reported 43 new errors on
unchanged code. An unpinned `pip install ruff` in CI is a build that can
go red without anyone touching the repo. Both versions now agree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
